#
# ── Lodgist Commit Message Template ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Reference: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
#
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#   <BLANK LINE>
#   <body>
#   <BLANK LINE>
#   <footer>
#
# ── Types (Conventional Commits) ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Changes to user-facing code:
#   feat        New feature (triggers minor version bump)
#   fix         Bug fix (triggers patch version bump)
#   perf        Performance improvement (triggers patch version bump)
#
# Changes that do NOT affect production code:
#   docs        Documentation only (README, API docs, guides)
#   style       Formatting, whitespace, missing semicolons; no logic change
#   refactor    Code restructure without feature/fix intent (rename, extract)
#   test        Adding/refactoring tests; no production code change
#   build       Build system or external dependency changes
#   ci          CI/CD config, scripts, pipeline changes
#   chore       Maintenance tasks, tooling, config; no production code change
#
# ── Scopes (Lodgist) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   frontend      Next.js app-router frontend
#   backend       Express API, services, middleware
#   db            Prisma schema, migrations, seeds
#   infra         AWS CDK, App Runner, RDS
#   auth          NextAuth, WebAuthn, RBAC, session
#   payments      Paystack integration, escrow, webhooks
#   bookings      Booking flow, concierge, tenancy agreements
#   verification  Land registry, trust safety engine, fraud detection
#   listings      Listing CRUD, search, detail pages
#   docs          README, BETA_STATUS, AGENTS, engineering plans
#   config        Env vars, tooling config, workspace settings
#   packages      Shared monorepo packages (ai-core, db, ui, etc.)
#
# ── Rules ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Subject : ≤ 50 chars · imperative mood ("add" not "added") · no period
#   Body    : wrap at 72 chars · explain WHAT and WHY (not HOW)
#   Footer  : reference issues (Closes: #N, Ref: #N) · mark BREAKING CHANGE
#
#   Breaking change in subject: append ! after type/scope
#     e.g. feat(payments)!: remove deprecated v1 verify endpoint
#   Breaking change in footer (when body is needed):
#     BREAKING CHANGE: <description of what breaks and migration path>
#
# ── Edge Cases ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Multiple unrelated changes → split into separate commits
#   WIP / partial commit    → use "wip:" prefix (squash before merge)
#   Co-authored commits     → add Co-authored-by: name <email> in footer
#   Reverts                 → use "revert:" type + reference original SHA
#   Subject > 50 chars      → move detail to body; subject is summary only
#
# ── Example ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# feat(payments): add Paystack escrow verification endpoint
#
# Implements /api/payments/verify to confirm Paystack transaction
# references on booking confirmation. Validates HMAC signature,
# transitions escrow state to HELD, and triggers concierge SMS.
#
# BREAKING CHANGE: Existing bookings without paystack_reference will
#   require data migration to populate the column.
# Closes: #189
#
# ── Your commit message starts below ──
